# Code owners. The owner is a required reviewer ONLY for:
# (a) GUARDRAILS: anything that, if changed, could weaken an agent guardrail
#     or stop a required check protecting us (CLAUDE.md, .claude/, floors, the
#     CI-config files that decide pass or fail, the workflows that enforce a
#     required check or deploy, CODEOWNERS and its proof test).
# (b) HUMAN-FACING DOCS: the owner's marketing, product and legal prose
#     (home, about, solutions, privacy, terms, LICENSE, NOTICE, README).
# EVERYTHING ELSE is released and lands on agent review plus green CI: the
# Dockerfile, deploy compose, .npmrc, package.json, workspace file, components,
# route table, mail-sending code, public files, and the Dependabot settings.
# Owner ruling. GitHub applies the LAST matching pattern. No catch-all line.
# The shared standards lines (SYNC-1) stay the final lines.

# 1. Guardrails: agent guidance, floors, CI-config files, and the tests of them.
**/CLAUDE.md                          @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.claude/                             @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/tools/floors.tsv                     @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/vitest.config.ts                     @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/playwright.config.ts                 @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.pre-commit-config.yaml              @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.prettierignore                      @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.gitignore                           @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/eslint.config.js                     @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/tsconfig.json                        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
# ci.yml carries both required checks and the deploy on push; the local actions it
# calls run inside those jobs. codeql.yml grants a write permission, so it stays
# owned. The other two workflow callers come from the shared lines at the end.
# dependabot.yml is released.
/.github/workflows/ci.yml             @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.github/workflows/codeql.yml         @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.github/actions/                     @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/app/lib/codeowners-ownership.test.ts @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/app/lib/ci-*.test.ts                 @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
**/CODEOWNERS                         @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# 2. The owner's words: marketing, product and legal text.
/app/routes/home.tsx                  @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/app/routes/about.tsx                 @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/app/routes/solutions.*.tsx           @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/app/routes/privacy.tsx               @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/app/routes/terms.tsx                 @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/LICENSE                              @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/NOTICE.md                            @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/README.md                            @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# Standards template lines (SYNC-1): these seven stay the final lines of this file.
# No /.github/ catch-all: it would own dependabot.yml, which is released.
/.standardsignore        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.standards.mode         @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.docs-lint*             @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.standards-db-tooling   @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.github/CODEOWNERS      @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.github/workflows/standards.yml  @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.github/workflows/docs-lint.yml  @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
